/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  extract02_declared_interior  --  the interior the case declares

  PHYSICALLY THIS IS `extract01_ethanol_water_benzene`: the same feed, the
  same benzene solvent, the same five theoretical stages, the same UNIFAC.
  The answer is the same answer.  What differs is where the cascade STARTS.

  A state directory is a RESTARTABLE SNAPSHOT.  `0/` carries one file per
  stream -- the boundary -- and, under `internalStates/`, one file per unit:
  what the equipment holds between them.  This case declares

      0/internalStates/extractor01

  a `stageProfile` block carrying the extract and raffinate leaving each of
  the five stages with their compositions, in exactly the grammar the run
  writes to `converged/internalStates/extractor01`.  THE SAME OBJECT TRAVELS
  BOTH WAYS: run the case, copy the file from `converged/` into `0/`, and the
  next run starts where the last one finished.

  A DECLARED PROFILE THAT DOES NOT SATISFY THE BALANCES IS A SEED, NOT AN
  ANSWER.  Nothing checks this file against the stage equilibria -- the sweeps
  do, and they move off any profile that is wrong.  What IS checked is that
  the declaration describes THIS cascade: the stage count, the component set,
  every value finite, no negative flow.  A mismatch REFUSES by name.

  Both routes announce, on every run:

      [seed] interior read from 0/ (stageProfile): 5 stages, extract F ...
      [seed] interior seeded by the unit: the fresh solvent as every stage's
             extract, the feed as every stage's raffinate -- declare a
             stageProfile block in 0/internalStates/<SECTOR>/<unit> to own it

  TRY IT: read the `iterations` KPI here, then delete `0/internalStates/` and
  run again.  Both runs reach the same cascade; only one had to search for it.
  `bin/choupo-init0` materialises the unit's OWN seed (the fresh solvent and
  the raw feed on every stage) -- never a better guess chosen for you.

  Record: docs/design/a-state-directory-is-a-restartable-snapshot.md
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

// stream state lives on disk in 0/ (per-stream files); flowsheetDict is TOPOLOGY only

units
(
    {
        name        extractor01;
        type        extractor;
        inputs      ( feed  solvent );        // feed at stage 1, solvent at stage N
        outputs     ( extract  raffinate );   // extract leaves stage 1, raffinate stage N

        operation
        {
            stages       5;
            solvent      benzene;             // defines the extract phase
            temperature  298.15 K;
        }
    }
);
